re [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7324" :question/id #uuid "8bec3fc3-9136-583c-81f6-756eaeed751b" :question/math-academy-id "q-7324" :question/problem "Express $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={30}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {30}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}=2\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7324/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "143766e0-0ef5-5caf-b699-d394d4a707e9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7324"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-65614/selection/ea0c6a210cef5aaaec265550038e8be7f82f94253d318de1e2a3faa814ba65fc" :answer/id #uuid "af5d382c-98ca-54a0-9c21-06d0795f6384" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{sin}^{2}⁡{40}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65614/selection/850faee0e72f31ad2db59a4aeceef6fac94fbaca3f8ded70ef48ec8c660e65c4" :answer/id #uuid "7001b475-d922-57ee-8574-c6d799309249" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡{80}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65614/selection/d9d1e60f1615c946c401d33d1bea863922a4fbfaaf8a3a639bc6e951599bf0fc" :answer/id #uuid "1a197143-ec2c-5a8e-ba31-6659239a871f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡{40}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65614/selection/53f654385ade084b300491a17946af11de2de9ce063eac8d58658d4af0cec03d" :answer/id #uuid "a9330c30-7093-5ea5-ae50-c2e0f22d89fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{80}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65614/selection/2959602d8b55e1bf8b608c4ce5745796ea433e14d30b5de3eaff03ad3c96b2cd" :answer/id #uuid "e4eb6d0c-2996-52f5-a261-6c1ef2915eca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{40}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65614/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c337c7fa-8444-5814-8527-8a4b7e8fa281" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-65614/selection/ea0c6a210cef5aaaec265550038e8be7f82f94253d318de1e2a3faa814ba65fc" :answer-field/choices ["q-65614/selection/ea0c6a210cef5aaaec265550038e8be7f82f94253d318de1e2a3faa814ba65fc" "q-65614/selection/850faee0e72f31ad2db59a4aeceef6fac94fbaca3f8ded70ef48ec8c660e65c4" "q-65614/selection/d9d1e60f1615c946c401d33d1bea863922a4fbfaaf8a3a639bc6e951599bf0fc" "q-65614/selection/53f654385ade084b300491a17946af11de2de9ce063eac8d58658d4af0cec03d" "q-65614/selection/2959602d8b55e1bf8b608c4ce5745796ea433e14d30b5de3eaff03ad3c96b2cd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-65614" :question/id #uuid "5d204ecc-cb39-533f-b52f-797be3e191c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-65614" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{80}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{cot}⁡{40}^{∘}}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={40}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {40}^{∘})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{40}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{40}^{∘}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{80}^{∘}=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{40}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{40}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nRewriting the given expression using the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{80}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{cot}⁡{40}^{∘}} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{40}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{40}^{∘}}{\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{40}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{40}^{∘}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{sin}^{2}⁡{40}^{∘}\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{40}^{∘}}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{40}^{∘}}} \\\\  & =2{sin}^{2}⁡{40}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-65614/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65614"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-24642"] :question/problem "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ in the denominator, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}}{2\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-65612/selection/aeccacb43dcd2a9a856aca5c2e949b7f3455840bd6624ecc28300f78dbdfc9a3" :answer/id